			"notes": "## What's Changed\n* feat: support for neoforge 1.21.1, migrate enchantments to data-driven by @logandhillon in https://github.com/logandhillon/mo_enchants/pull/21\n\n## Changelog\n- The mod has been upgraded to NeoForge.\n- Updated internal systems and compatibility layers to support the latest modding environment.\n- Migrated enchantment systems to a new, more reliable framework\n- Improved enchantment event handling and performance.\n- Improved critical damage effects with new particle feedback.\n- Updated enchantment IDs to better match their names.\n- Updated generated data and mod metadata.\n\n---\n\n## Technical Changelog\n\n### Breaking Changes\n- Changed enchantment registry IDs to match enchantment names.\n- Renamed `enchantment.helper` package to `event`.\n- Migrated the project from Forge to NeoForge.\n- Updated Gradle tooling and build configuration.\n\n### Architecture Changes\n- Decentralized the event dispatcher system.\n- Migrated event handling infrastructure to NeoForge APIs.\n- Migrated:\n  - Blocks\n  - GLMs\n  - Init systems\n  - Utility classes\n  - Events\n  - Data generation\n  - Enchantment systems\n\n### Enchantment System Migration\n- Migrated enchantments to the new effect-based architecture\n\n### New Technical Features\n- Added `CriticallyDamageEntity` enchantment effect.\n- Added critical hit particle effects.\n- Added event handlers for migrated enchantment behaviors.\n- Updated data generation pipeline.\n\n### Build & Metadata\n- Upgraded Gradle to 9.6.1.\n- Updated mod metadata.\n- Removed legacy Forge run configurations.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/logandhillon/mo_enchants/compare/v1.6.4+1.20.1...v2.0.0+1.21.1"
		},
